{
 "_comment": [
  "The CRS legislative-subject vocabulary as OBSERVED LIVE from",
  "api.congress.gov during story 5.5 (2026-10-19). Not a published list:",
  "the API exposes no vocabulary endpoint (checked: /v3/bill/subjects,",
  "/v3/subject and /v3/legislative-subject all 404), so this is the set of",
  "distinct `legislativeSubjects[].name` values seen across:",
  "",
  "  * ~1,400 bills sampled at random (seed 11) from 8,468 listed bills of",
  "    the 117th, 118th and 119th Congresses, types hr/s/hjres/sjres; and",
  "  * all 889 distinct measures that received a recorded House roll-call",
  "    vote in the 118th and 119th Congresses (the population story 5.5",
  "    actually serves).",
  "",
  "WHAT IT IS FOR. `test_every_mapped_crs_term_was_observed_in_real_data`",
  "asserts every key of SUBJECT_TERM_TO_SUBTOPIC appears here. That test",
  "exists because the first draft of the mapping table contained",
  "'Broadband and internet access' -- a string that reads exactly like a CRS",
  "term and is not one. Eighteen such invented or misremembered keys were",
  "caught this way and corrected to their real equivalents (e.g.",
  "'Prescription drug costs' -> 'Prescription drugs', 'Education funding' ->",
  "'Education programs funding'). An invented key is silent dead code that",
  "makes a reviewer believe the table covers a subtopic it does not.",
  "",
  "NOT EXHAUSTIVE, and does not need to be: it is a lower bound used to",
  "refute invented keys, never to authorise them. A real CRS term absent",
  "here simply cannot be added to the mapping table without first being",
  "observed, which is the conservative direction."
 ],
